\pard \fs24\tx-955\tx-720\tx0\tx342\tx1062\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\tx9360\tx10080\tx10800\tx11520\tx12240\tx12960\tx13680\tx14400\tx15120\tx15840\tx16560\tx17280\tx18000\tx18720
{\plain \fs36 \f2\fs36 Preface to the Ordination Rites}{\plain \fs24 \f2 \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f2  \par
}{\plain \fs20 \f2\fs20 The Holy Scriptures and ancient Christian writers make it clear that from the \softline
apostles{\u8217\'92} time, there have been different ministries within the Church. In \softline
particular, since the time of the New Testament, three distinct orders of ordained \softline
ministers have been characteristic of Christ's holy catholic Church. First, there is \softline
the order of bishops who carry on the apostolic work of leading, supervising, and \softline
uniting the Church. Secondly, associated with them are the presbyters, or \softline
ordained elders, in subsequent times generally known as priests. Together with the \softline
bishops, they take part in the governance of the Church, in the carrying out of its \softline
missionary and pastoral work, and in the preaching of the Word of God and \softline
administering his holy Sacraments. Thirdly, there are deacons who assist bishops \softline
and priests in all of this work. It is also a special responsibility of deacons to \softline
minister in Christ's name to the poor, the sick, the suffering, and the helpless.\par
}\pard \fs20\sl120\slmult1\tx-955\tx-720\tx0\tx342\tx1062\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\tx9360\tx10080\tx10800\tx11520\tx12240\tx12960\tx13680\tx14400\tx15120\tx15840\tx16560\tx17280\tx18000\tx18720 
{\plain \fs20 \f2\fs20  \par
}\pard \fs20\tx-955\tx-720\tx0\tx342\tx1062\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\tx9360\tx10080\tx10800\tx11520\tx12240\tx12960\tx13680\tx14400\tx15120\tx15840\tx16560\tx17280\tx18000\tx18720
{\plain \fs20 \f2\fs20 The persons who are chosen and recognized by the Church as being called by \softline
God to the ordained ministry are admitted to these sacred orders by solemn \softline
prayer and the laying on of episcopal hands.  It has been, and is, the intention \softline
and purpose of this Church to maintain and continue these three orders; and for \softline
this purpose these services of ordination and consecration are appointed.  No \softline
persons are allowed to exercise the offices of bishop, priest, or deacon in this \softline
Church unless they are so ordained, or have already received such ordination with \softline
the laying on of hands by bishops who are themselves duly qualified to confer \softline
Holy Orders.\par
}\pard \fs20\sl120\slmult1\tx-955\tx-720\tx0\tx342\tx1062\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\tx9360\tx10080\tx10800\tx11520\tx12240\tx12960\tx13680\tx14400\tx15120\tx15840\tx16560\tx17280\tx18000\tx18720 
{\plain \fs20 \f2\fs20  \par
}\pard \fs24\tx-955\tx-720\tx0\tx342\tx1062\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\tx9360\tx10080\tx10800\tx11520\tx12240\tx12960\tx13680\tx14400\tx15120\tx15840\tx16560\tx17280\tx18000\tx18720
{\plain \fs20 \f2\fs20 It is also recognized and affirmed that the threefold ministry is not the exclusive \softline
property of this portion of Christ's catholic Church, but }{\plain \fs20 \f2\fs20 is a gift from God for \softline
the nurture of his people and the proclamation of his Gospel everywhere. \softline
Accordingly, the manner of ordaining in this Church is to be such as has been, \softline
and is, most generally recognized by Christian people as suitable for the \softline
conferring of the sacred orders of bishop, priest, and deacon. }{\plain \fs24 \f2 \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f2 \par
}\column 
\pard \fs36\tx-955\tx-720\tx0\tx342\tx1062\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\tx9360\tx10080\tx10800\tx11520\tx12240\tx12960\tx13680\tx14400\tx15120\tx15840\tx16560\tx17280\tx18000\tx18720
{\plain \fs36 \i\f2\fs36 Concerning the\par
}{\plain \fs36 \i\f2\fs36 Ordination of a Bishop}{\plain \fs24 \f2 \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f2 \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f2 \par
}{\plain \fs20 \f2\fs20 In accordance with ancient custom, it is desirable, if possible, that\par
}{\plain \fs20 \f2\fs20 bishops be ordained on Sundays and other feasts of our Lord or on the\par
}{\plain \fs20 \f2\fs20 feasts of apostles or evangelists.\par
}\pard \fs20\sl120\slmult1\tx-955\tx-720\tx0\tx342\tx1062\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\tx9360\tx10080\tx10800\tx11520\tx12240\tx12960\tx13680\tx14400\tx15120\tx15840\tx16560\tx17280\tx18000\tx18720 
{\plain \fs20 \f2\fs20  \par
}\pard \fs20\tx-955\tx-720\tx0\tx342\tx1062\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\tx9360\tx10080\tx10800\tx11520\tx12240\tx12960\tx13680\tx14400\tx15120\tx15840\tx16560\tx17280\tx18000\tx18720
{\plain \fs20 \f2\fs20 When a bishop is to be ordained, the Presiding Bishop of the Church,\par
}{\plain \fs20 \f2\fs20 or a bishop appointed by the Presiding Bishop, presides and serves as\par
}{\plain \fs20 \f2\fs20 chief consecrator.  At least two other bishops serve as co-consecrators.\par
}{\plain \fs20 \f2\fs20 Representatives of the presbyterate, diaconate, and laity of the diocese\par
}{\plain \fs20 \f2\fs20 for which the new bishop is to be consecrated, are assigned appropriate\par
}{\plain \fs20 \f2\fs20 duties in the service.\par
}\pard \fs20\sl120\slmult1\tx-955\tx-720\tx0\tx342\tx1062\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\tx9360\tx10080\tx10800\tx11520\tx12240\tx12960\tx13680\tx14400\tx15120\tx15840\tx16560\tx17280\tx18000\tx18720 
{\plain \fs20 \f2\fs20  \par
}\pard \fs20\tx-955\tx-720\tx0\tx342\tx1062\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\tx9360\tx10080\tx10800\tx11520\tx12240\tx12960\tx13680\tx14400\tx15120\tx15840\tx16560\tx17280\tx18000\tx18720
{\plain \fs20 \f2\fs20 From the beginning of the service until the Offertory, the chief\par
}{\plain \fs20 \f2\fs20 consecrator presides from a chair placed close to the people, so that\par
}{\plain \fs20 \f2\fs20 all may see and hear what is done.  The other bishops, or a convenient\par
}{\plain \fs20 \f2\fs20 number of them, sit to the right and left of the chief consecrator.\par
}\pard \fs20\sl120\slmult1\tx-955\tx-720\tx0\tx342\tx1062\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\tx9360\tx10080\tx10800\tx11520\tx12240\tx12960\tx13680\tx14400\tx15120\tx15840\tx16560\tx17280\tx18000\tx18720 
{\plain \fs20 \f2\fs20  \par
}\pard \fs20\tx-955\tx-720\tx0\tx342\tx1062\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\tx9360\tx10080\tx10800\tx11520\tx12240\tx12960\tx13680\tx14400\tx15120\tx15840\tx16560\tx17280\tx18000\tx18720
{\plain \fs20 \f2\fs20 The bishop-elect is vested in a rochet or alb, without stole, tippet,\par
}{\plain \fs20 \f2\fs20 or other vesture distinctive of ecclesiastical or academic rank or order.\par
}\pard \fs20\sl120\slmult1\tx-955\tx-720\tx0\tx342\tx1062\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\tx9360\tx10080\tx10800\tx11520\tx12240\tx12960\tx13680\tx14400\tx15120\tx15840\tx16560\tx17280\tx18000\tx18720 
{\plain \fs20 \f2\fs20  \par
}\pard \fs20\tx-955\tx-720\tx0\tx342\tx1062\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\tx9360\tx10080\tx10800\tx11520\tx12240\tx12960\tx13680\tx14400\tx15120\tx15840\tx16560\tx17280\tx18000\tx18720
{\plain \fs20 \f2\fs20 When the bishop-elect is presented, his full name (designated by the\par
}{\plain \fs20 \f2\fs20 symbol }{\plain \fs20 \i\f2\fs20 N.N}{\plain \fs20 \f2\fs20 .) is used.  Thereafter, it is appropriate to refer to him only by the \softline
Christian name by which he wishes to be known.\par
}\pard \fs20\sl120\slmult1\tx-955\tx-720\tx0\tx342\tx1062\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\tx9360\tx10080\tx10800\tx11520\tx12240\tx12960\tx13680\tx14400\tx15120\tx15840\tx16560\tx17280\tx18000\tx18720 
{\plain \fs20 \f2\fs20  \par
}\pard \fs20\tx-955\tx-720\tx0\tx342\tx1062\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\tx9360\tx10080\tx10800\tx11520\tx12240\tx12960\tx13680\tx14400\tx15120\tx15840\tx16560\tx17280\tx18000\tx18720
{\plain \fs20 \f2\fs20 At the Offertory, it is appropriate that the bread and wine be brought\par
}{\plain \fs20 \f2\fs20 to the Altar by the family or friends of the newly ordained.\par
}\pard \fs20\sl120\slmult1\tx-955\tx-720\tx0\tx342\tx1062\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\tx9360\tx10080\tx10800\tx11520\tx12240\tx12960\tx13680\tx14400\tx15120\tx15840\tx16560\tx17280\tx18000\tx18720 
{\plain \fs20 \f2\fs20  \par
}\pard \fs20\tx-955\tx-720\tx0\tx342\tx1062\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\tx9360\tx10080\tx10800\tx11520\tx12240\tx12960\tx13680\tx14400\tx15120\tx15840\tx16560\tx17280\tx18000\tx18720
{\plain \fs20 \f2\fs20 The family of the newly ordained may receive Communion before other members \softline
of the congregation. Opportunity is always given to the people to communicate.\par
